&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Old Mission does not seek capital from outside investors, allowing us the flexibility to aggressively invest in our team members and keep them engaged in the firm’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About This Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Compensation Manager to lead compensation strategy and operations for the firm. This role owns the day-to-day design, analysis, and administration of our pay programs - from market benchmarking to pay equity to merit cycles - and serves as the go-to expert on compensation matters for HR and business leaders. You&#39;ll have real ownership over how we pay people, with the opportunity to shape and mature our total rewards programs as the firm grows. Just as important, this is a people-facing role. You&#39;ll sit across from candidates, employees, and managers to explain and, where appropriate, negotiate compensation directly - listening closely, building trust, and gathering the context that leads to better pay decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with leadership in designing, benchmarking, and managing competitive compensation structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage bonus and promotion cycles, including budget modeling and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze compensation trends and present findings/recommendations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support benefits program administration and vendor relationships (with room to shape broader total rewards strategy over time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for compensation questions from employees, managers, and HR partners, and guide them through pay decisions in direct conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate compensation decisions and the reasoning behind them directly to candidates and employees, and help shape how the firm frames and delivers pay conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support compensation negotiations for offers, promotions, and retention, balancing individual expectations against internal budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listen for and surface the information gathered during compensation conversations, feeding those insights back into strategy, program design, and market positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the company&#39;s participation in compensation surveys and lead market benchmarking for all roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards and reporting for compensation and total rewards metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in compensation, HR analytics, or a related total rewards function&lt;/li&gt;
